.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509_VERIFY 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509_verify ,
.Nm X509_self_signed ,
.Nm X509_REQ_verify_ex ,
.Nm X509_REQ_verify ,
.Nm X509_CRL_verify ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_verify
.Nd verify certificate, certificate request, or CRL signature
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509.h
.Ft int
.Fo X509_verify
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_self_signed
.Fa "X509 *cert"
.Fa "int verify_signature"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_REQ_verify_ex
.Fa "X509_REQ *a"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_REQ_verify
.Fa "X509_REQ *a"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *r"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_CRL_verify
.Fa "X509_CRL *a"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *r"
.Fc
.In openssl/x509_acert.h
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ACERT_verify
.Fa "X509_CRL *a"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *r"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn X509_verify
verifies the signature of certificate
.Fa x
using public key
.Fa pkey .
Only the signature is checked: no other checks (such as certificate
chain validity) are performed.
.Pp
.Fn X509_self_signed
checks whether certificate
.Fa cert
is self-signed.
For success the issuer and subject names must match, the components of
the authority key identifier (if present) must match the subject key
identifier etc.
The signature itself is actually verified only if
.Fa verify_signature
is 1, as for explicitly trusted certificates this verification is not
worth the effort.
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_verify_ex ,
.Fn X509_REQ_verify ,
.Fn X509_CRL_verify
and
.Fn X509_ACERT_verify
verify the signatures of certificate requests, CRLs and attribute
certificates respectively.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn X509_verify ,
.Fn X509_REQ_verify_ex ,
.Fn X509_REQ_verify
and
.Fn X509_CRL_verify
return 1 if the signature is valid and 0 if the signature check fails.
If the signature could not be checked at all because it was ill-formed,
the certificate or the request was not complete or some other error
occurred then -1 is returned.
.Pp
.Fn X509_self_signed
returns the same values but also returns 1 if all respective fields
match and
.Fa verify_signature
is 0.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr d2i_X509 3 ,
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr X509_CRL_get0_by_serial 3 ,
.Xr X509_get0_signature 3 ,
.Xr X509_get_ext_d2i 3 ,
.Xr X509_get_extension_flags 3 ,
.Xr X509_get_pubkey 3 ,
.Xr X509_get_subject_name 3 ,
.Xr X509_get_version 3 ,
.Xr X509_NAME_ENTRY_get_object 3 ,
.Xr X509_NAME_get_index_by_NID 3 ,
.Xr X509_NAME_print_ex 3 ,
.Xr X509V3_get_d2i 3 ,
.Xr X509_verify_cert 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_LIB_CTX 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn X509_verify ,
.Fn X509_REQ_verify ,
and
.Fn X509_CRL_verify
functions are available in all versions of OpenSSL.
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_verify_ex ,
and
.Fn X509_self_signed
were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
.Fn X509_ACERT_verify
was added in OpenSSL 3.4.
